**Read:** [Tratamento de Minérios — CETEM, sixth edition](../sources/Tratamento-de-Minerios-CETEM.lingua#r_04ZQFADZ3NC3T6QDPQ565W1ERA), the complete mineral-characterization, sampling, and relevant process chapters; [Tratamento de Minérios: Práticas Laboratoriais — Sampaio, França, and Braga](../sources/CETEM-Praticas-Laboratoriais.lingua#r_44AAWXB1D7MBR9B0V3TYB8GF9B), the complete corresponding testwork methods; [Usinas de Beneficiamento de Minérios do Brasil — CETEM](../sources/CETEM-Usinas-de-Beneficiamento.lingua#r_62ZD994C9YYXB1YDVFQST5B27J), the full selected case and its references; [Relate mineral associations to liberation without mistaking a section for every particle](../../../../gaia/earth/mineralogy-and-petrology/applications/Grain-associations-liberation-and-process-mineralogy.lingua#r_03BD9ADDV2B62T8RF26S61R77C), the shared association/measurement-support explanation.

Geometallurgy relates geological/mineralogical variability to extraction, fragmentation, concentration, product quality, utilities, and waste behavior. A grade domain and a processing-response domain can differ. Mineral hosts, texture, hardness, alteration, contaminants, and water chemistry may influence response independently of bulk valuable-element content.

Testwork requires representative material, preparation, method, scale, operating conditions, and uncertainty. A single favorable specimen or batch test cannot establish every block's response. Correlating response with a geological label needs a designed population and independent validation rather than automatic extrapolation.

Connect domains with the resource model, process assumptions, sampling support, and schedule. Blending or changing feed can alter recovery, throughput, product, and water/reagent demand nonlinearly. A reported recovery is conditional on the feed, method, and boundaries used.

**Work:** reconstruct a complete characterization/testwork case from geological samples through mineral association and process results. Compare two plausible domains or response models, test an independent sample/condition, and explain the consequence for a production or product-quality account. Identify where data are sparse or proprietary and what original test could address the gap.

Read full CETEM characterization and laboratory methods plus the complete selected plant case. Preserve the handoff between geological evidence and engineering response rather than substituting a commodity-average recovery for the investigated material.

**Continue:** [Analyze cutoff decisions with explicit costs, recovery, quality, and constraints](../planning/Cutoff-grades-value-and-capacity-constraints.lingua#r_2D0X3JWGVJ02492M19S11CBP25).

**Return:** [Mining and mineral engineering — extraction, processing, and continuing work](../Mining-and-mineral-engineering.lingua#r_22HJPS3RTK5EX1J55YJP75PHYA).
